  "content": {
    "title": "Florida vs Iowa score, highlights: Hawkeyes upset Gators on game-winning 3-pointer",
    "text": "Updated March 22, 2026, 10:43 p.m. ETFollow all of Sunday's NCAA Tournament second round games with USA TODAY Sports' live updates.Iowa basketball busted some brackets on Sunday, March 22, against No. 1 Florida.The No. 9 seed Hawkeyes upset Florida 73-72 in the second round of the NCAA Tournament after Alvaro Folgueiras nailed a game-winning 3-pointer with four seconds remaining to defeat the defending national champions. The win sets up a matchup against No. 4 seed Nebraska in the Sweet 16, in a battle that will feature a whole lot of corn.First-year coach Ben McCollum has now taken Iowa to its first Sweet 16 since 1999, a feat Fran McCaffery surprisingly never accomplished during his long tenure. McCollum, only in his second season coaching at the Division I level, already has three NCAA Tournament wins.HIT REFRESH FOR UPDATES. Florida vs Iowa scoreTEAMS1H2HFIowa334073Florida314172 Iowa heads to Sweet 16 for the first time since 1999The top upset of the NCAA Tournament so far goes to Iowa, courtesy of a wild game-winning shot by Alvaro Folgueiras on Iowa's final possession.Florida didn't get a shot off on its final possession. Iowa takes the lead!Wow, Alvaro Folgueiras sinks a 3-pointer to give Iowa a 73-72 lead with four seconds left. What a shot in a huge moment. Bennett Stirtz misses go-ahead layupIowa gets a possession down 71-70 with no shot clock, but Bennett Stirtz driving layup misses and Florida grabs the rebound. Florida makes one of two ensuing free-throw attempts to extend its lead to 72-70 with 8.9 seconds left.Iowa is going to have another shot. Can Stirtz capitalize on the second chance? Cooper Koch is on fire from 3-point rangeFlorida takes a 65-61 lead, looking like it was about to take over the game. However, Iowa isn't going down without a fight. Bennett Stirtz is fouled and nails a pair of free throws before Cooper Koch makes his fourth 3-pointer of the second half to give the Hawkeyes a 66-65 lead with 3:55 left.This one is going to come down to the wire, folks. Iowa takes 61-60 leadFlorida briefly takes a 60-58 lead, but Iowa immediately answers with another 3-pointer by Cooper Koch, his third of the game. Iowa leads 61-60 with 6:35 left in regulation.This game is turning into a banger. Florida pulls within a pointFlorida only trails 57-56 after Xaivian Lee nails a 25-foot 3-pointer, which forces an Iowa timeout. The Gators are on a 17-6 run since coach Todd Golden last called a timeout following an Iowa run. Iowa keeping Florida bigs in checkFlorida has arguably the best frontcourt in college basketball, but Iowa has shut them down so far. Thomas Haugh and Alex Condon have 12 and 11 points, respectively, although Haugh only has one field goal with the rest of his points coming from the free-throw line. Rueben Chinyelu has no points on one shot attempt.Florida is shooting 44% from the field and is 4-of-13 from 3-point range. Florida calls timeout after Iowa runIowa is on a 13-2 run and takes a 51-39 lead with 14:11 left after Cooper Koch nails a 3-pointer, which forces a Florida timeout. Tavion Banks leads all scorers with 18 points for the Hawkeyes.Florida is in trouble and needs to act fast in order to avoid upset. Iowa leads Florida 33-31 at halftimeIowa has Florida on upset watch, as it takes a 33-31 lead into halftime after Kael Combs' sinks a 7-foot floater just before the buzzer to break the tie.Iowa's Tavion Banks was hot in the first half, and leads all scorers with 14 points, even though he has missed three free throws already. Star guard Bennett Stirtz is 3-of-7 shooting with six points, four rebounds and two assists. Iowa defense is swarmingIowa is hanging with Florida in the first half, thanks to its defense holding quite strong against the Gators. Florida is shooting 33% from the field, and Iowa is ahead 28-25 with less than three minutes left in the first half. Iowa pushes lead to double digitsIowa is sticking around, and the lead is now up to double digits. Tavion Banks and Bennett Stirtz continue to impress, and the Hawkeyes have the No. 1 seed on early upset watch. Hawkeyes off to a hot start vs the champsWhat time is Florida vs Iowa?Time: 7:10 p.m. ET, Sunday.What channel is Iowa vs Florida? How to watch, streaming infoThe game is airing on TBS, streaming via Fubo.Florida vs Iowa prediction, oddsOdds provided by BetMGM, as of 1 p.m., Sunday.∎ Andrew Abadie, Gainesville Sun: Florida 84, Iowa 73The storyline of this matchup will be the two contrasting tempos between Iowa and Florida. The Gators play a much faster pace compared to the Hawkeyes. Look for Xaivian Lee and Boogie Fland to have big games as this matchup will be a test for the duo. Even with Iowa playing at a slower tempo, Florida's front court has a clear advantage.∎ Tyler Tachman, Des Moines Register: Florida 86, Iowa 70While Iowa has had a solid first season under Ben McCollum, the dream of a deep March run ends here. The Gators are simply too deep and too consistent. The loss to Vandy in the SEC Tournament was a bit of a wake-up call, plus this is essentially a home game for the Gators, since it's being played in Tampa. Expect the reigning champs to come out determined to repeat and send the Hawkeyes home.John Leuzzi: FloridaJordan Mendoza: FloridaEhsan Kassim: FloridaBlake Schuster: FloridaMoneyline: Florida (-550); Iowa (+400)Spread: Florida (-9.5)Over/under total: 145.5Olivier Rioux height: How tall is Number 32 on Florida?Earlier this season, Florida 7-9 center Olivier Rioux became the tallest player to play in an NCAA basketball game.He broke the mark of Manut Bol, who was 7-7 and played at Division II Bridgeport.",
